"# Create an order

\`POST /orders/{storeId}\`

Operation ID: \`createOrder\`

Tags: \`orders\`

Creates a new order.

## Servers

- \`https://api.example.com\`

## Authentication

This operation requires:

- \`bearer\` (HTTP bearer)

## Parameters

### Path parameters

- \`storeId\` (string, required)
  Store ID.

### Query parameters

- \`dryRun\` (boolean, default: \`false\`)

## Request body (required)

### Content type: \`application/json\`

Schema: \`object\`

- \`id\` (string<ulid>, read-only)
  ID.
- \`orderItems\` (object[], required, min items: 1)
  List of items to include in the order.
  - \`orderItems[].quantity\` (integer, required, >= 1)
    Quantity of the menu item.
  - \`orderItems[].comment\` (string, max length: 500)

Example:

\`\`\`json
{
  \\"orderItems\\": [
    {
      \\"quantity\\": 2
    }
  ]
}
\`\`\`

## Responses

### 201

Order created.

Response headers:

- \`X-Request-Id\` (string)
  Request ID.

#### Content type: \`application/json\`

Schema: \`object\`

- \`id\` (string<ulid>, read-only)
  ID.
- \`orderItems\` (object[], required, min items: 1)
  List of items to include in the order.
  - \`orderItems[].quantity\` (integer, required, >= 1)
    Quantity of the menu item.
  - \`orderItems[].comment\` (string, max length: 500)

### 400

Bad request.
"
